---
// A sketch of the idea in the COLM paper: context is a second axis for test-time scaling.
---

<figure class="axes">
  <svg viewBox="0 0 420 260" role="img" aria-label="Two axes. Horizontal: test-time compute, longer reasoning, more samples, more search. Vertical: context built from experience, which the paper scales instead.">
    <defs>
      <marker id="ah" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="8" refX="6" refY="4" orient="auto">
        <path d="M0,0 L8,4 L0,8 z" fill="currentColor" />
      </marker>
    </defs>
    <g class="ink3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#ah)">
      <path d="M50,210 H390" />
      <path d="M50,210 V30" />
    </g>
    <g class="ink2" font-size="12">
      <text x="220" y="240" text-anchor="middle">Test-time compute: longer reasoning, more samples, more search</text>
      <text transform="translate(22,120) rotate(-90)" text-anchor="middle">Context: distilled experience</text>
    </g>
    <g class="muted" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="4 4">
      <path d="M60,200 C150,185 250,180 360,178" />
    </g>
    <g class="accent" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5">
      <path d="M60,200 C70,120 100,70 150,55" marker-end="url(#ah)" />
    </g>
    <g font-size="12">
      <text class="muted" x="270" y="170" text-anchor="middle">more compute: cost up, much of it wasted</text>
      <text class="accent" x="160" y="48">this paper: better context, same compute</text>
    </g>
  </svg>
  <figcaption>Experience is distilled into lessons, consolidated so memory stays small, and organized as a concept tree for retrieval.</figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .axes {
    margin: 0;
  }
  svg {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    display: block;
    font-family: var(--sans);
  }
  .ink2 {
    color: var(--ink-2);
    fill: var(--ink-2);
  }
  .ink3 {
    color: var(--rule-strong);
  }
  .muted {
    color: var(--mark-muted);
    fill: var(--mark-muted);
  }
  .accent {
    color: var(--accent);
    fill: var(--accent);
  }
  figcaption {
    margin-top: 6px;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--ink-3);
  }
</style>
